 s/2024/03/2023-09-19-Levy-Astral.wavs-0317.jpg
UID:6xcFjmgyomKsV0B-29PbM
SUMMARY:Texas Sound Meditation with Leala and James
DTSTAMP:20260802T054431Z
DTSTART:20260804T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Levy Park brings “Self Care” to a whole new level with Sound He
	aling led by Leala and James. \nA sound bath is a gentle\, nurturing\, and
	 cathartic meditation experience for anyone looking to improve the quality
	 of their life. This act of self-care is beneficial for anyone from beginn
	ers to advanced meditators who are ready to experience a greater sense of 
	peace and well-being. \nThe Levy Park Sound Baths will assist in clearing 
	out that which is blocking the natural vitality while strengthening the co
	nnection and balance between mind\, body\, and soul. A collectively cultiv
	ated safe space offers participants an opportunity to deepen their own jou
	rney of self-love\, healing or transformation. \nWhile relieving stress\, 
	tension and anxiety this sound immersion experience will have you feeling 
	revitalized\, relaxed and rejuvenate. Let the sounds wash away everything 
	that no longer serves you as you set your intentions and manifest your des
	ires! \n* Formerly Astral.WAVZ Sound Therapy\n\nhttps://www.levyparkhousto
	n.org/events/sound-therapy-texas-sound-2/2026-08-04/\n\nFrom Levy Park Hou
	ston
URL:https://www.levyparkhouston.org/events/sound-therapy-texas-sound-2/2026
	-08-04/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:levy-park-houston
CATEGORIES:Levy Park Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston
 .com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/The-Girl-on-the-Train-at-Alley-Theatre.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston.com/wp-content/uploads
 /2026/07/The-Girl-on-the-Train-at-Alley-Theatre.jpg
UID:OpylFNaqhllMiOKzllbWl
SUMMARY:The Girl on the Train at Alley Theatre
DTSTAMP:20260802T054431Z
DTSTART:20260804T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Alley Theatre presents The Girl on the Train\, the 2026 product
	ion in Alley’s annual Summer Chills series\, live on stage in Downtown. \n
	The modern psychological thriller\, adapted from the best-selling novel an
	d hit film\, follows Rachel\, a woman struggling with dependency. \nShe mu
	st piece together her fragmented memories to find a girl who’s gone missin
	g. As her night comes back to her\, she considers\, “Who can you trust whe
	n you can’t trust yourself?” \nAdmission\nTickets start at $32. Order tick
	ets or learn more. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by th
	e event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details
	. \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or o
	ffer across all of our channels. \n\nhttps://365thingsinhouston.com/calend
	ar/the-girl-on-the-train-at-alley-theatre-13/\n\nFrom 365 Things to Do in 
	Houston
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/the-girl-on-the-train-at-alley-
	theatre-13/
LOCATION:Alley Theatre\, 615 Texas St\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United State
	s
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:365-things-houston
CATEGORIES:365 Things to Do in Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston
 .com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/52nd-Annual-Houston-Shakespeare-Festival-T
 he-Comedy-of-Errors-at-Miller-Outdoor-Theatre.jpeg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston.com/wp-content/uploads
 /2026/07/52nd-Annual-Houston-Shakespeare-Festival-The-Comedy-of-Errors-at-
 Miller-Outdoor-Theatre.jpeg
UID:E47RGLFp4ZSdl2PuH2dpg
SUMMARY:52nd Annual Houston Shakespeare Festival: The Comedy of Errors at M
	iller Outdoor Theatre
DTSTAMP:20260802T054431Z
DTSTART:20260804T201500Z
DESCRIPTION:Houston Shakespeare Festival\, the city’s annual summer theater
	 tradition\, celebrates its 52nd season with performances of both The Temp
	est and The Comedy of Errors on alternating nights at Miller Outdoor Theat
	re. \nShakespeare’s Comedy of Errors\nShakespeare’s riotous farce of mista
	ken identity\, The Comedy of Errors\, brings double trouble to the bustlin
	g port city of Ephesus when two sets of twins—separated at birth—unexpecte
	dly cross paths\, unleashing a whirlwind of mayhem and mirth. \nIn this fa
	st-paced comedy bursting with physical humor\, outrageous confusion\, and 
	joyful surprise\, husbands are mistaken for strangers\, servants are denie
	d their own names\, and no one can tell friend from foe. As misunderstandi
	ngs multiply and tempers flare\, the laughter never lets up. \nFinding You
	r Seat at Miller Outdoor Theatre\nAs always\, all seats at Miller are free
	\, but covered seating for popular evening shows usually requires a free a
	ssigned ticket reserved 24 hours in advance. \nLearn more about getting fr
	ee seated tickets at Miller. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more or reserve a fr
	ee seated ticket. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the
	 event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details.
	  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or o
	ffer across all of our channels.\n\nhttps://365thingsinhouston.com/calenda
	r/52nd-annual-houston-shakespeare-festival-the-comedy-of-errors-at-miller-
	outdoor-theatre-2/\n\nFrom 365 Things to Do in Houston
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/52nd-annual-houston-shakespeare
	-festival-the-comedy-of-errors-at-miller-outdoor-theatre-2/
LOCATION:Miller Outdoor Theatre\, 6000 Hermann Park Dr\, Houston\, TX\, 770
	30\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:365-things-houston
CATEGORIES:365 Things to Do in Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
